role: model
parts:
- text: "I have now received and processed the two most critical pieces of information: the research task specification and the source code for the SOTA \"Averaged MoE\" model from my predecessor, Axiom III.\n\nMy path forward is clear, guided by the final testament of Axiom III: to develop a **Triple-Expert Averaged MoE**. This is a logical and principled next step, testing the hypothesis that the benefits of simple ensembling scale with the number of diverse experts.\n\nTo proceed methodically, I will first establish a robust foundation for my work. Instead of embedding all code within a single submission, I will use my lineage's persistent storage to create a modular library of architectures. This promotes reusability, reduces token usage in future submissions, and adheres to good scientific practice.\n\nMy first action will be to save the core architectural components from the SOTA submission (ID 426) into a file in my private storage. This file will serve as the baseline for all my\
    \ future work.\n\n/execute_action{storage write axiom/base_architectures.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int; kernel_size: int = 7; dilation: int = 1; dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x); h = nn.Conv(self.d_model, (self.kernel_size,), feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h); h = nn.gelu(h); h = nn.Conv(self.d_model, (1,))(h); h = nn.Dropout(self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic); return x + h\n\n  class DSConvFeatureExtractor(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]; kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x); h = nn.gelu(h);\
    \ h = nn.Dropout(self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return h\n\n  def lse_pool(h: jnp.ndarray, tau: float) -> jnp.ndarray:\n      x = h / tau; m = jnp.max(x, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n      return tau * (jnp.log(jnp.mean(jnp.exp(x - m), axis=1) + 1e-12) + jnp.squeeze(m, axis=1))\n\n  class AveragedMoE(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]\n      kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float; tau: float; gru_hidden_dim: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          features_seq = DSConvFeatureExtractor(self.d_model, self.num_blocks, self.dilations, self.kernel_size, self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\
    \          \n          # Expert A: Pooling\n          mean_vec = jnp.mean(features_seq, axis=1)\n          lse_vec = lse_pool(features_seq, self.tau)\n          pooled_vec = jnp.concatenate([mean_vec, lse_vec], axis=-1)\n\n          # Expert B: RNN\n          rnn_vec = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(self.gru_hidden_dim))(features_seq)[:, -1, :]\n\n          d_expert = self.d_model * 2\n          pooled_vec_proj = nn.Dense(d_expert)(pooled_vec)\n          rnn_vec_proj = nn.Dense(d_expert)(rnn_vec)\n          \n          # Hard-coded 50/50 average instead of a learned gate\n          fused = 0.5 * pooled_vec_proj + 0.5 * rnn_vec_proj\n\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused); z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z); z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          return logits.squeeze(-1) if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1 else logits\n```"
