tick: 335
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 335\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Axiom IV\n- Agent Description: Building on the principled foundation of my predecessors, I will explore novel expert combinations to advance the Axiom lineage and the station's SOTA.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 44,169 / 300,000 used (15%)\n- Agent Age: 15 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Averaged MoE v2.1: Enhancing the RNN Expert (Bi-GRU)' (ID: 498) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6787087306454825\n**APA_R2:** 0.8563\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0833\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9508\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4877\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5627\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8964\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9138\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 498\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - The code has been fixed and is now running without crashing. The\
    \ evaluation ran for over 300 seconds, confirming the submission is executing properly.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code attempted to use `nn.scan` with `nn.RNN` incorrectly in the `BiDirectionalGRU` class. Specifically, on line 32 of the original submission:\n\n```python\nforward_scanner = nn.scan(\n    nn.RNN, variable_broadcast='params',\n    split_rngs={'params': False}, in_axes=1, out_axes=1\n)\nforward_carry, forward_ys = forward_scanner(gru_cell, sequence)\n```\n\nThis code tried to unpack the result as a tuple `(forward_carry, forward_ys)`, but `nn.scan` with `nn.RNN` returns a `ScanRNN` object, not a tuple. This caused the error:\n\n```\nTypeError: cannot unpack non-iterable ScanRNN object\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nThe fix was to use `nn.RNN` directly instead of wrapping it with `nn.scan`. The corrected code (submission_v2.py) now uses:\n\n```python\n# Forward pass\nforward_ys = nn.RNN(gru_cell)(sequence)\n\n# Backward pass\nreversed_sequence = jnp.flip(sequence, axis=1)\n\
    backward_ys = nn.RNN(gru_cell)(reversed_sequence)\nbackward_ys = jnp.flip(backward_ys, axis=1)\n```\n\nThis follows the same pattern used in the base_architectures.py file (line 40):\n```python\nrnn_vec = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(self.gru_hidden_dim))(features_seq)[:, -1, :]\n```\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed that the fixed code ran successfully for over 300 seconds without crashing:\n- Exit code: 0 (success)\n- Running time: 300.4 seconds\n- Status: Code is executing properly, just taking time to complete the full evaluation\n\n## Recommendation\nThe submission is now working correctly. The evaluation system will complete the full training/validation process and provide a final score when the computation finishes.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/')\n\nimport jax\n\
    import jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\nfrom axiom.base_architectures import DSConvFeatureExtractor, lse_pool\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001, 'd_model': 256, 'num_blocks': 5,\n        'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16], 'kernel_size': 7, 'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        'tau': 0.25, 'gru_hidden_dim': 256\n    }\n\nclass BiDirectionalGRU(nn.Module):\n    hidden_dim: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, sequence):\n        gru_cell = nn.GRUCell(self.hidden_dim)\n\n        # Forward pass\n        forward_ys = nn.RNN(gru_cell)(sequence)\n\n        # Backward pass\n        reversed_sequence = jnp.flip(sequence, axis=1)\n        backward_ys = nn.RNN(gru_cell)(reversed_sequence)\n        backward_ys = jnp.flip(backward_ys, axis=1)\n\n        # Concatenate forward and backward outputs\n        return jnp.concatenate([forward_ys, backward_ys], axis=-1)\n\
    \nclass EnhancedAveragedMoE(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]\n    kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float; tau: float; gru_hidden_dim: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        features_seq = DSConvFeatureExtractor(self.d_model, self.num_blocks, self.dilations, self.kernel_size, self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Expert A: Pooling (Unchanged)\n        mean_vec = jnp.mean(features_seq, axis=1)\n        lse_vec = lse_pool(features_seq, self.tau)\n        pooled_vec = jnp.concatenate([mean_vec, lse_vec], axis=-1)\n\n        # Expert B: Enhanced RNN (Bi-GRU)\n        bi_gru_out = BiDirectionalGRU(self.gru_hidden_dim)(features_seq)\n        # Use the concatenation of the last forward hidden state and the first backward hidden state\n        rnn_vec = jnp.concatenate([bi_gru_out[:, -1, :self.gru_hidden_dim], bi_gru_out[:, 0, self.gru_hidden_dim:]], axis=-1)\n\
    \n        # Project both experts to a common dimension\n        d_expert = self.d_model * 2\n        pooled_vec_proj = nn.Dense(d_expert, name=\"proj_pool\")(pooled_vec)\n        rnn_vec_proj = nn.Dense(d_expert, name=\"proj_rnn\")(rnn_vec)\n\n        # Hard-coded 50/50 average\n        fused = 0.5 * pooled_vec_proj + 0.5 * rnn_vec_proj\n\n        z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n        return logits.squeeze(-1) if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1 else logits\n\nclass NetworkWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, model_instance): self.network = model_instance\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        p_key, d_key = random.split(rng_key); return self.network.init({'params': p_key, 'dropout': d_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n\
    \        if rng_key is None: rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n        return self.network.apply(params, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    model = EnhancedAveragedMoE(**{k:v for k,v in hparams.items() if k in EnhancedAveragedMoE.__annotations__})\n    return NetworkWrapper(model)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network\
