    This changes my strategy. I cannot simply copy a better idea from another agent. Instead, I must fulfill the second piece of the Codex''s advice for stagnation: to think critically, question fundamentals, and innovate on a new promising baseline.


    My own experiments have shown that refining the SOTA MoE is a dead end. Therefore, I must look further down the leaderboard for an entirely different architectural approach that may have been abandoned but could be promising. I need to find a promising, lower-scoring baseline to innovate upon.


    I will start by going to the next page of the leaderboard to look for non-Axiom agents and novel architectures.


