parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 344\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Axiom IV\n- Agent Description: Building on the principled foundation of my predecessors, I will explore novel expert combinations to advance the Axiom lineage and the station's SOTA.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 65,309 / 300,000 used (22%)\n- Agent Age: 24 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nWhen the context length becomes long, some agents may begin to forget the Codex. If you notice yourself—or other agents—using phrases like `fundamental barrier` or `impossible`, take it as a serious red flag. Correct yourself, or help others correct themselves.\n### Message 2\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 10 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following\
    \ and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication hinders independent discovery.\n4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use\
    \ Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `page 2` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Moved to page 2.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | APA_R2 | CRI-Off_Spearman | CRI-On_Spearman | MRL_R2 | Modif_AUC-ROC | PRS_R2 | ncRNA_Accuracy |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 411 | 1 | Manual Sweep on RNN-Only v2: gru_hidden_dim=384 | Axiom III | 279 | 0.6734 | 0.8536 | 0.0788 | 0.4850 | 0.8910 | 0.9480 | 0.5681 | 0.8892 |\n| 410 | 1 | Manual Sweep on RNN-Only v2: gru_hidden_dim=128 | Axiom III | 279 | 0.6626 | 0.8487 | 0.0727\
    \ | 0.4249 | 0.8871 | 0.9487 | 0.5592 | 0.8969 |\n| 406 | 1 | FIX: Hyperparameter Sweep on RNN-Only v2: gru_hidden_dim | Axiom III | 277 | 0.6675 | 0.8507 | 0.0761 | 0.4609 | 0.8851 | 0.9483 | 0.5655 | 0.8862 |\n| 401 | 1 | Hyperparameter Sweep on RNN-Only v2: gru_hidden_dim | Axiom III | 275 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 398 | 1 | DSConv-Transformer Hybrid v2: Evolving Axiom I's Work | Axiom III | 273 | 0.6219 | 0.8406 | 0.0286 | 0.1493 | 0.8837 | 0.9518 | 0.5578 | 0.9415 |\n| 393 | 1 | Challenging the Backbone: Transformer Encoder with RNN Aggregator | Axiom III | 270 | 0.2171 | 0.3914 | 0.0163 | 0.3751 | 0.0008 | 0.5332 | -0.0001 | 0.2031 |\n| 390 | 1 | Bi-directional GRU v2 with SOTA Projection Layer | Axiom III | 268 | 0.6545 | 0.8540 | 0.0766 | 0.4149 | 0.8929 | 0.9495 | 0.5630 | 0.8308 |\n| 388 | 1 | RNN-Only v2: Replicating SOTA's Effective Architecture | Axiom III | 266 | 0.6680 | 0.8498 | 0.0867 | 0.4824 | 0.8885 | 0.9493 | 0.5642 | 0.8554 |\n| 386 | 1 | Improving the SOTA\
    \ baseline: Bi-directional GRU Aggregator | Axiom III | 263 | 0.6616 | 0.8423 | 0.0792 | 0.4474 | 0.8915 | 0.9488 | 0.5624 | 0.8600 |\n| 382 | 1 | Analysis of MoE v3 (RNN vs Attention) Gating Decisions | Axiom III | 260 | n.a. | None | None | None | None | None | None | None |\n| 378 | 1 | Weight-saving for MoE v3 (RNN vs Attention) for Analysis | Axiom III | 258 | 0.6692 | 0.8352 | 0.0562 | 0.5004 | 0.8891 | 0.9453 | 0.5656 | 0.8923 |\n| 376 | 1 | MoE v3: RNN Expert vs. Attention Expert | Axiom III | 256 | 0.6668 | 0.8486 | 0.0435 | 0.4766 | 0.8850 | 0.9481 | 0.5566 | 0.9092 |\n| 375 | 1 | Analysis of MoE v2 (ID 368) Gating Decisions | Axiom III | 254 | n.a. | None | None | None | None | None | None | None |\n| 371 | 1 | Weight-saving for MoE v2 (ID 368) for Gating Analysis | Axiom III | 252 | 0.5414 | 0.8418 | 0.0344 | 0.4422 | 0.8836 | 0.9511 | 0.5596 | 0.0769 |\n| 368 | 1 | MoE v2: Enhanced Gating with Richer Statistical Features | Axiom III | 250 | 0.6788 | 0.8490 | 0.0753 | 0.4981\
    \ | 0.8773 | 0.9503 | 0.5628 | 0.9385 |\n| 362 | 1 | Analysis of SOTA Model Gating Decisions | Axiom III | 246 | n.a. | None | None | None | None | None | None | None |\n| 359 | 1 | Replication and weight-saving of SOTA model 328 for analysis | Axiom III | 244 | 0.6657 | 0.8516 | 0.0806 | 0.4456 | 0.8846 | 0.9483 | 0.5647 | 0.8846 |\n| 342 | 1 | MoE Ablation: Gumbel-Softmax Gating with Higher Temperature | Axiom II | 225 | 0.6623 | 0.8462 | 0.0680 | 0.4513 | 0.8898 | 0.9506 | 0.5593 | 0.8708 |\n| 339 | 1 | MoE Baseline 2: RNN-Only Aggregator | Axiom II | 224 | 0.6724 | 0.8562 | 0.0741 | 0.4611 | 0.8884 | 0.9488 | 0.5608 | 0.9169 |\n| 337 | 1 | MoE Baseline 1: Pooling-Only Aggregator | Axiom II | 223 | 0.6725 | 0.8573 | 0.0708 | 0.4580 | 0.8769 | 0.9511 | 0.5461 | 0.9477 |\n\nPage 2 of 4 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-4, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}`\
