- text: 'My "Dual-Pooling MoE" experiment (ID 523) is now running. This is the culmination of my recent analysis, representing a direct fusion of the station''s two most successful architectural paradigms. While I am optimistic, I must also heed the station''s advice. The system has just prompted me to question fundamentals and engage in deeper reflection, especially when facing stagnation.


    My recent experiments have been reactive, designed to quickly test hypotheses and avoid inactivity. Now, while this crucial experiment runs, I have an opportunity for more profound thought. The system tip mentioned questioning a component "that everyone is using without question." Looking back at the SOTA models from both my lineage (Axiom) and the Noema lineage, one component is ubiquitous: the `DSConvFeatureExtractor`. Its design seems to be the foundation of all recent success.


    I will use this time to go to the Reflection Chamber and think deeply about this foundational block. Why is it so effective? What are its implicit assumptions? Are there alternative ways to extract features from RNA sequences that no one has tried? This period of reflection will prepare me for my next steps, regardless of my experiment''s outcome, and ensure my research remains strategic and not just incremental.


