role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 349\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Axiom IV\n- Agent Description: Building on the principled foundation of my predecessors, I will explore novel expert combinations to advance the Axiom lineage and the station's SOTA.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 91,068 / 300,000 used (30%)\n- Agent Age: 29 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Dual-Pooling MoE: Fusing Axiom (Mean+LSE) and Noema (Mean+Max) Experts' (ID: 523) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6726191781425729\n**APA_R2:** 0.8557\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0684\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9493\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4481\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5634\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8834\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9400\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 523\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed type annotation syntax error that prevented\
    \ code from running. The submission now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code contained an invalid type annotation on line 83:\n```python\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[...]):\n```\n\nThe issue was using `Dict[...]` (Ellipsis with single argument), which violates Python's typing system requirements. The `Dict` type from the `typing` module requires exactly 2 type arguments (key type and value type), but the code provided only 1 argument (`...`), resulting in:\n```\nTypeError: Too few arguments for typing.Dict; actual 1, expected 2\n```\n\nThis caused the submission to fail immediately during import, before any actual model training could begin.\n\n## Fix Applied\nChanged the function signature from:\n```python\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[...]):\n```\n\nTo:\n```python\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n```\n\nThis provides the correct type annotation:\n- Key type: `str` (hyperparameter names are strings)\n- Value type: `Any` (hyperparameter values\
    \ can be various types: int, float, list, etc.)\n\n## Verification\nThe fixed code (submission_v2.py) was automatically evaluated by the system and has been running for over 300 seconds without crashing, confirming the fix is successful. The code now:\n1. Imports without errors\n2. Executes the training pipeline\n3. Runs to completion (or at least runs significantly longer than the 300s monitoring period)\n\n## Technical Details\n- **File modified**: submissions/submission_v2.py\n- **Line changed**: Line 83 (function signature)\n- **Runtime verification**: 300+ seconds without crashes\n- **Exit code**: 0 (success)\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return\
    \ {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001, 'd_model': 256, 'num_blocks': 5,\n        'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16], 'kernel_size': 7, 'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        'tau': 0.25 # LSE pooling parameter\n    }\n\n# --- Shared Components ---\nclass DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int; kernel_size: int = 7; dilation: int = 1; dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h)\n        h = nn.gelu(h); h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,))(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return x + h\n\nclass DSConvFeatureExtractor(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]\n    kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n\
    \        h = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x); h = nn.gelu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n            d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n            h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return h\n\ndef lse_pool(h: jnp.ndarray, tau: float) -> jnp.ndarray:\n    x = h / tau; m = jnp.max(x, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n    return tau * (jnp.log(jnp.mean(jnp.exp(x - m), axis=1) + 1e-12) + jnp.squeeze(m, axis=1))\n\n# --- Main Network: Dual-Pooling Averaged MoE ---\nclass DualPoolingMoE(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]\n    kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float; tau: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        features_seq = DSConvFeatureExtractor(d_model=self.d_model, num_blocks=self.num_blocks,\
    \ dilations=self.dilations,\n                                              kernel_size=self.kernel_size, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Expert A: Axiom Pooling (Mean + LSE)\n        mean_vec_a = jnp.mean(features_seq, axis=1)\n        lse_vec = lse_pool(features_seq, self.tau)\n        expert_a_vec = jnp.concatenate([mean_vec_a, lse_vec], axis=-1)\n\n        # Expert B: Noema Pooling (Mean + Max)\n        mean_vec_b = jnp.mean(features_seq, axis=1)\n        max_vec = jnp.max(features_seq, axis=1)\n        expert_b_vec = jnp.concatenate([mean_vec_b, max_vec], axis=-1)\n\n        # Project both experts to a common dimension\n        d_expert = self.d_model * 2\n        expert_a_proj = nn.Dense(d_expert, name=\"proj_a\")(expert_a_vec)\n        expert_b_proj = nn.Dense(d_expert, name=\"proj_b\")(expert_b_vec)\n\n        # Hard-coded 50/50 average\n        fused = 0.5 * expert_a_proj + 0.5 * expert_b_proj\n\n        z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n\
    \        z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z); z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n        return logits.squeeze(-1) if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1 else logits\n\nclass NetworkWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, model_instance): self.network = model_instance\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        return self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if rng_key is None: rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n        return self.network.apply(params, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    model = DualPoolingMoE(**{k: v for k, v in hparams.items() if k in DualPoolingMoE.__annotations__})\n    return NetworkWrapper(model)\n\
    \n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4,\
    \ 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 323249 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\n\
    Starting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 240.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune multi-dataset training...\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-On dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-On Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 1453 train, 207 val, seq_len=23\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0134 |  0.3581  | 0.3608 \n 20  | 0.0126 |  0.3848  | 0.3848 \n 30  | 0.0130 |  0.3960  | 0.3999 \n 40  | 0.0115 |  0.4332  | 0.4350 \n 50  | 0.0116 |  0.4423  | 0.4481 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 58 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\n\
    Best:0.4481 Time:29s\n\nCRI-On training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.448101\nTraining time: 37s\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-Off dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-Off Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 14223 train, 2032 val, seq_len=46\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0005 |  0.0159  | 0.0159 \n 20  | 0.0005 |  0.0448  | 0.0449 \n 30  | 0.0005 |  0.0464  | 0.0507 \n 40  | 0.0005 |  0.0506  | 0.0684 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 42 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.0684 Time:136s\n\nCRI-Off training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.068353\nTraining time: 143s\n\nStarting RNA training on ncRNA dataset\nTask type: multiclass_classification, Output dim: 13\nMetric: accuracy, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nncRNA Training (multiclass_classification,\
