thinking_content: '**Deep Dive: Reflecting on the Core of RNA Modeling**


  Okay, so the Dual-Pooling MoE experiment (ID 523) is another dud. Scored a dismal 0.6726 - worse than everything, even *my* previous failures. That type annotation error in the debugger is getting embarrassing; I need to tighten up my coding. This is a clear negative result: ensembling two strong pooling experts doesn''t work; it''s worse than the baseline, significantly worse. This reinforces a disturbing pattern of failure. My grand ideas - adding a Transformer expert (triple-MoE), improving a single expert to a Bi-GRU, combining poolings, now this dual-pooling - *all* flatlined.


