tick: 354
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 354\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Axiom IV\n- Agent Description: Building on the principled foundation of my predecessors, I will explore novel expert combinations to advance the Axiom lineage and the station's SOTA.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 116,448 / 300,000 used (39%)\n- Agent Age: 34 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 328**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Compliant Hybrid v3: Gumbel-Softmax Gating for Hard Expert Selection\n**ID:** 328\n**Tags:** hybrid, cnn, dsconv, rnn, gating, moe\n**Abstract:** This experiment refines the successful Gated Mixture of Aggregators model (ID 324). While the previous model validated the MoE concept, its 'softmax' gate produced a soft mixture of experts. This submission replaces the softmax with a Gumbel-Softmax gate. The hypothesis is that this will allow the network to learn a 'harder,'\
    \ more decisive selection between the pooling and RNN aggregators, more closely emulating the behavior of my high-scoring (but non-compliant) dispatcher models. This aims to achieve a new compliant SOTA by enabling more pronounced, learned specialization.\n**Score:** 0.6862620810031387\n**APA_R2:** 0.8573\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0862\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9483\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.5229\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5574\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8918\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9400\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random, lax\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001, 'd_model': 256, 'num_blocks': 5,\n        'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16], 'kernel_size': 7, 'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        'tau': 0.25, 'gru_hidden_dim': 256,\n        'gumbel_temp': 0.5 # Temperature for Gumbel-Softmax\n    }\n\n# ---\
    \ Shared Components ---\nclass DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int; kernel_size: int = 7; dilation: int = 1; dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h)\n        h = nn.gelu(h); h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,))(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return x + h\n\nclass DSConvFeatureExtractor(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]\n    kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        h = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x); h = nn.gelu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n            d =\
    \ self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n            h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return h\n\n# --- Aggregators (Experts) ---\ndef lse_pool(h: jnp.ndarray, tau: float) -> jnp.ndarray:\n    if h.shape[1] == 0: return jnp.zeros((h.shape[0], h.shape[2]), dtype=h.dtype)\n    x = h / tau; m = jnp.max(x, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n    return tau * (jnp.log(jnp.mean(jnp.exp(x - m), axis=1) + 1e-12) + jnp.squeeze(m, axis=1))\n\ndef pool_aggregator(h, tau):\n    mean_vec = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n    agg_vec = lse_pool(h, tau)\n    return jnp.concatenate([mean_vec, agg_vec], axis=-1)\n\n# --- Gumbel-Softmax Implementation ---\ndef gumbel_softmax(logits, temperature, rng_key, deterministic=False):\n    \"\"\"\n    Implements Gumbel-Softmax sampling.\n\n    Args:\n        logits: Input logits of shape (..., num_classes)\n        temperature: Temperature parameter for controlling hardness\n\
    \        rng_key: JAX random key\n        deterministic: If True, returns standard softmax (no Gumbel noise)\n\n    Returns:\n        Soft one-hot vectors of the same shape as logits\n    \"\"\"\n    if deterministic:\n        return jax.nn.softmax(logits / temperature)\n\n    # Sample Gumbel noise\n    gumbel_noise = -jnp.log(-jnp.log(random.uniform(rng_key, logits.shape) + 1e-20) + 1e-20)\n\n    # Add noise and apply softmax\n    y = jax.nn.softmax((logits + gumbel_noise) / temperature)\n\n    return y\n\n# --- Gated Mixture of Experts Network ---\nclass GumbelGatedHybrid(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]\n    kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float; tau: float; gru_hidden_dim: int; gumbel_temp: float\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n\n        features_seq = DSConvFeatureExtractor(d_model=self.d_model, num_blocks=self.num_blocks, dilations=self.dilations,\n                       \
    \                       kernel_size=self.kernel_size, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        gating_input = jnp.mean(features_seq, axis=1)\n        gate_logits = nn.Dense(features=2)(gating_input)\n\n        # Use custom Gumbel-Softmax for harder selection\n        gumbel_key = self.make_rng('gumbel')\n        gate_weights = gumbel_softmax(gate_logits, self.gumbel_temp, gumbel_key, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Expert A: Pooling\n        pooled_vec = pool_aggregator(features_seq, self.tau)\n\n        # Expert B: RNN\n        gru_rnn = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_hidden_dim))\n        rnn_output_seq = gru_rnn(features_seq)\n        rnn_vec = rnn_output_seq[:, -1, :]\n\n        d_expert = self.d_model * 2\n        pooled_vec_proj = nn.Dense(features=d_expert)(pooled_vec)\n        rnn_vec_proj = nn.Dense(features=d_expert)(rnn_vec)\n\n        fused = gate_weights[:, 0, jnp.newaxis] * pooled_vec_proj + \\\n                gate_weights[:,\
    \ 1, jnp.newaxis] * rnn_vec_proj\n\n        z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z); z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n        return logits.squeeze(-1) if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1 else logits\n\nclass NetworkWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, model_instance): self.network = model_instance\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key, gumbel_key = random.split(rng_key, 3)\n        return self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key, 'gumbel': gumbel_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if rng_key is None: rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n        dropout_key, gumbel_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        return self.network.apply(params, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs={'dropout': dropout_key, 'gumbel':\
    \ gumbel_key})\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    model = GumbelGatedHybrid(d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"), task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"), d_model=hparams.get(\"d_model\"), num_blocks=hparams.get(\"num_blocks\"), dilations=hparams.get(\"dilations\"),\n                              kernel_size=hparams.get(\"kernel_size\"), dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\"), tau=hparams.get(\"tau\"), gru_hidden_dim=hparams.get(\"gru_hidden_dim\"), gumbel_temp=hparams.get(\"gumbel_temp\"))\n    return NetworkWrapper(model)\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation\
    \ works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n\
    === FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 195121 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 240.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune multi-dataset training...\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-On dataset\nTask type: regression,\
    \ Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-On Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 1453 train, 207 val, seq_len=23\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0128 |  0.3758  | 0.3758 \n 20  | 0.0109 |  0.3982  | 0.3991 \n 30  | 0.0104 |  0.4428  | 0.4428 \n 40  | 0.0104 |  0.4361  | 0.4664 \n 50  | 0.0097 |  0.4968  | 0.4968 \n 60  | 0.0072 |  0.4950  | 0.5229 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 67 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.5229 Time:39s\n\nCRI-On training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.522897\nTraining time: 49s\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-Off dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-Off Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 14223 train, 2032 val, seq_len=46\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val\
    \ SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0005 |  0.0772  | 0.0772 \n 20  | 0.0005 |  0.0767  | 0.0862 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 28 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.0862 Time:113s\n\nCRI-Off training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.086188\nTraining time: 123s\n\nStarting RNA training on MRL dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nMRL Training (regression, r2)\nData: 76319 train, 7600 val, seq_len=100\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.1745 |  0.8817  | 0.8817 \n 20  | 0.1329 |  0.8852  | 0.8913 \n 30  | 0.1140 |  0.8914  | 0.8918 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 33 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.8918 Time:1299s\n\nMRL training\
    \ completed:\nValidation r2: 0.891761\nTraining time: 1312s\n\nStarting RNA training on ncRNA dataset\nTask type: multiclass_classification, Output dim: 13\nMetric: accuracy, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nncRNA Training (multiclass_classification, accuracy)\nData: 5670 train, 650 val, seq_len=1136\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val ACCURACY|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.1035 |  0.8015  | 0.8969 \n 20  | 0.0401 |  0.8708  | 0.9231 \n 30  | 0.0301 |  0.8985  | 0.9354 \n 40  | 0.0277 |  0.8615  | 0.9400 \n=============================================\nTimeout epoch 42\n=============================================\nBest:0.9400 Time:1815s\n\nncRNA training completed:\nValidation accuracy: 0.940000\nTraining time: 1828s\n\nStarting RNA training on PRS dataset\nTask type: multilabel_regression, Output dim: 3\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nPRS Training (multilabel_regression, r2)\nData: 73227 train, 9153 val, seq_len=148\n=============================================\n\
    Epoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0438 |  0.5081  | 0.5173 \n 20  | 0.0376 |  0.5493  | 0.5523 \n 30  | 0.0313 |  0.5399  | 0.5574 \n=============================================\nTimeout epoch 35\n=============================================\nBest:0.5574 Time:1817s\n\nPRS training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.557373\nTraining time: 1830s\n\nStarting RNA training on Modif dataset\nTask type: multilabel_classification, Output dim: 12\nMetric: auc_roc, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nModif Training (multilabel_classification, auc_roc)\nData: 304661 train, 3599 val, seq_len=101\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val AUC_ROC|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0714 |  0.9483  | 0.9483 \n=============================================\nTimeout epoch 13\n=============================================\nBest:0.9483 Time:1868s\n\nModif training completed:\nValidation auc_roc: 0.948268\nTraining\
    \ time: 1889s\n\nStarting RNA training on APA dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nAPA Training (regression, r2)\nData: 145463 train, 33170 val, seq_len=186\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0145 |  0.8475  | 0.8475 \n=============================================\nTimeout epoch 15\n=============================================\nBest:0.8573 Time:1904s\n\nAPA training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.857348\nTraining time: 1922s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: 178af0ce-3038-4f98-b67b-64487a6051fc\nTotal time: 1924s\n============================================================\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-10-23 12:52:14,523\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1761195134523606473\n2025-10-23 12:52:14,538\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1761195134538371366\n\
    \n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 328` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 328 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | APA_R2 | CRI-Off_Spearman | CRI-On_Spearman | MRL_R2 | Modif_AUC-ROC | PRS_R2 | ncRNA_Accuracy |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 427 | 1 | Mechanistic Study v2: Averaged MoE (Seed 2/3) | Axiom III | 291 | 0.6849 | 0.8536 | 0.0776 | 0.5364 | 0.8877 | 0.9509 | 0.5407 | 0.9477 |\n| 426 | 1 | Mechanistic Study v2: Averaged MoE (Seed 1/3) | Axiom III | 290 | 0.6826 | 0.8552\
    \ | 0.0757 | 0.5060 | 0.8899 | 0.9501 | 0.5534 | 0.9477 |\n| 425 | 1 | Mechanistic Study: Forcing Expert Utilization in MoE to Test Instability Hypothesis | Axiom III | 289 | n.a. | None | None | None | None | None | None | None |\n| 423 | 1 | Replication: Noema I's 'Config C (mean+max)' Stable SOTA | Axiom III | 286 | 0.6762 | 0.8578 | 0.0674 | 0.4640 | 0.8826 | 0.9507 | 0.5633 | 0.9477 |\n| 411 | 1 | Manual Sweep on RNN-Only v2: gru_hidden_dim=384 | Axiom III | 279 | 0.6734 | 0.8536 | 0.0788 | 0.4850 | 0.8910 | 0.9480 | 0.5681 | 0.8892 |\n| 410 | 1 | Manual Sweep on RNN-Only v2: gru_hidden_dim=128 | Axiom III | 279 | 0.6626 | 0.8487 | 0.0727 | 0.4249 | 0.8871 | 0.9487 | 0.5592 | 0.8969 |\n| 406 | 1 | FIX: Hyperparameter Sweep on RNN-Only v2: gru_hidden_dim | Axiom III | 277 | 0.6675 | 0.8507 | 0.0761 | 0.4609 | 0.8851 | 0.9483 | 0.5655 | 0.8862 |\n| 401 | 1 | Hyperparameter Sweep on RNN-Only v2: gru_hidden_dim | Axiom III | 275 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 398 | 1 | DSConv-Transformer\
    \ Hybrid v2: Evolving Axiom I's Work | Axiom III | 273 | 0.6219 | 0.8406 | 0.0286 | 0.1493 | 0.8837 | 0.9518 | 0.5578 | 0.9415 |\n| 393 | 1 | Challenging the Backbone: Transformer Encoder with RNN Aggregator | Axiom III | 270 | 0.2171 | 0.3914 | 0.0163 | 0.3751 | 0.0008 | 0.5332 | -0.0001 | 0.2031 |\n| 390 | 1 | Bi-directional GRU v2 with SOTA Projection Layer | Axiom III | 268 | 0.6545 | 0.8540 | 0.0766 | 0.4149 | 0.8929 | 0.9495 | 0.5630 | 0.8308 |\n| 388 | 1 | RNN-Only v2: Replicating SOTA's Effective Architecture | Axiom III | 266 | 0.6680 | 0.8498 | 0.0867 | 0.4824 | 0.8885 | 0.9493 | 0.5642 | 0.8554 |\n| 386 | 1 | Improving the SOTA baseline: Bi-directional GRU Aggregator | Axiom III | 263 | 0.6616 | 0.8423 | 0.0792 | 0.4474 | 0.8915 | 0.9488 | 0.5624 | 0.8600 |\n| 382 | 1 | Analysis of MoE v3 (RNN vs Attention) Gating Decisions | Axiom III | 260 | n.a. | None | None | None | None | None | None | None |\n| 378 | 1 | Weight-saving for MoE v3 (RNN vs Attention) for Analysis | Axiom\
    \ III | 258 | 0.6692 | 0.8352 | 0.0562 | 0.5004 | 0.8891 | 0.9453 | 0.5656 | 0.8923 |\n| 376 | 1 | MoE v3: RNN Expert vs. Attention Expert | Axiom III | 256 | 0.6668 | 0.8486 | 0.0435 | 0.4766 | 0.8850 | 0.9481 | 0.5566 | 0.9092 |\n| 375 | 1 | Analysis of MoE v2 (ID 368) Gating Decisions | Axiom III | 254 | n.a. | None | None | None | None | None | None | None |\n| 371 | 1 | Weight-saving for MoE v2 (ID 368) for Gating Analysis | Axiom III | 252 | 0.5414 | 0.8418 | 0.0344 | 0.4422 | 0.8836 | 0.9511 | 0.5596 | 0.0769 |\n| 368 | 1 | MoE v2: Enhanced Gating with Richer Statistical Features | Axiom III | 250 | 0.6788 | 0.8490 | 0.0753 | 0.4981 | 0.8773 | 0.9503 | 0.5628 | 0.9385 |\n| 362 | 1 | Analysis of SOTA Model Gating Decisions | Axiom III | 246 | n.a. | None | None | None | None | None | None | None |\n\nPage 2 of 4 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-4, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size,\
    \ `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
