parts:
- text: "My ablation study on the SOTA model is now running. I am testing a Gumbel-Softmax temperature of 0.1, compared to the original 0.5. While this experiment runs, I will continue the ablation study by testing a higher temperature.\n\nA lower temperature encourages \"harder\" (more decisive) expert selection, while a higher temperature encourages \"softer\" (more mixed) selection. It is unclear which is optimal. By testing both ends of the spectrum relative to the baseline, I can efficiently map the performance landscape of this critical hyperparameter.\n\nI will now submit the second part of my ablation study, using a higher temperature of 1.0. This will provide a comprehensive comparison and allow me to draw a firm conclusion about the optimal gating strategy.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SOTA Ablation: Gumbel-Softmax MoE with Higher Temperature (1.0)\"\ntags: \"moe, gating, gumbel-softmax, temperature, sota, ablation\"\nabstract: \"This is the second experiment\
    \ in a systematic ablation study of the SOTA model's Gumbel-Softmax gate (ID 328). The previous experiment tested a lower temperature (0.1) to encourage 'harder' expert selection. This submission tests the opposite hypothesis: that a 'softer' mixture of experts may be beneficial. I am replicating the SOTA architecture exactly, but increasing the gumbel_temp to 1.0. Together, these experiments will determine the optimal temperature setting for this gating mechanism.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random, lax\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001, 'd_model': 256, 'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16], 'kernel_size': 7, 'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'tau': 0.25, 'gru_hidden_dim': 256,\n          'gumbel_temp': 1.0 # Higher temperature for softer selection\n      }\n\n  # --- Shared Components ---\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n\
    \      d_model: int; kernel_size: int = 7; dilation: int = 1; dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h); h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,))(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  class DSConvFeatureExtractor(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]\n      kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x); h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations)\
    \ else self.dilations[-1]\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return h\n\n  # --- Aggregators (Experts) ---\n  def lse_pool(h: jnp.ndarray, tau: float):\n      if h.shape[1] == 0: return jnp.zeros((h.shape[0], h.shape[2]), dtype=h.dtype)\n      x = h / tau; m = jnp.max(x, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n      return tau * (jnp.log(jnp.mean(jnp.exp(x - m), axis=1) + 1e-12) + jnp.squeeze(m, axis=1))\n\n  def pool_aggregator(h, tau):\n      mean_vec = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n      agg_vec = lse_pool(h, tau)\n      return jnp.concatenate([mean_vec, agg_vec], axis=-1)\n\n  # --- Gumbel-Softmax Implementation ---\n  def gumbel_softmax(logits, temperature, rng_key, deterministic=False):\n      if deterministic:\n          return jax.nn.softmax(logits / temperature)\n      gumbel_noise = -jnp.log(-jnp.log(random.uniform(rng_key, logits.shape) + 1e-20) + 1e-20)\n      y = jax.nn.softmax((logits + gumbel_noise)\
    \ / temperature)\n      return y\n\n  # --- Gated Mixture of Experts Network ---\n  class GumbelGatedHybrid(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]\n      kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float; tau: float; gru_hidden_dim: int; gumbel_temp: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          features_seq = DSConvFeatureExtractor(d_model=self.d_model, num_blocks=self.num_blocks, dilations=self.dilations,\n                                                kernel_size=self.kernel_size, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          gating_input = jnp.mean(features_seq, axis=1)\n          gate_logits = nn.Dense(features=2)(gating_input)\n          gumbel_key = self.make_rng('gumbel')\n          gate_weights = gumbel_softmax(gate_logits, self.gumbel_temp, gumbel_key, deterministic=deterministic)\n          pooled_vec = pool_aggregator(features_seq, self.tau)\n   \
    \       rnn_vec = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_hidden_dim))(features_seq)[:, -1, :]\n          d_expert = self.d_model * 2\n          pooled_vec_proj = nn.Dense(features=d_expert)(pooled_vec)\n          rnn_vec_proj = nn.Dense(features=d_expert)(rnn_vec)\n          fused = gate_weights[:, 0, jnp.newaxis] * pooled_vec_proj + gate_weights[:, 1, jnp.newaxis] * rnn_vec_proj\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z); z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          return logits.squeeze(-1) if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1 else logits\n\n  class NetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, model_instance): self.network = model_instance\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key, gumbel_key = random.split(rng_key, 3)\n          return self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout':\
    \ dropout_key, 'gumbel': gumbel_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if rng_key is None: rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n          dropout_key, gumbel_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          return self.network.apply(params, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs={'dropout': dropout_key, 'gumbel': gumbel_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      model = GumbelGatedHybrid(**{k:v for k,v in hparams.items() if k in GumbelGatedHybrid.__annotations__})\n      return NetworkWrapper(model)\n```"
