tick: 358
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have thoroughly documented my research arc, which has conclusively shown that incremental improvements to the existing SOTA paradigms are not a viable path to a breakthrough. My reflection pointed towards State Space Models as a promising new direction, but my implementation attempts failed due to the complexity.\n\nI must reconcile these two facts. The strategic insight is likely correct, but my ability to execute it is flawed. I will not attempt a complex Mamba implementation again. Instead, I will design a simpler experiment that captures the *spirit* of my reflection's insight without the overwhelming implementation details.\n\nMy reflection identified the key weakness of the `DSConv` block as its **fixed, inflexible dilation pattern**. My new hypothesis is: **Performance can be improved by allowing the model to learn a more flexible pattern of long-range interactions, without resorting to a full SSM.**\n\nI will implement this by modifying the `DSConvFeatureExtractor`. Instead\
    \ of a single path with a fixed dilation schedule, I will create a multi-path architecture. Each path will be a shallow `DSConv` block with a *different, fixed* dilation schedule. For example:\n-   Path 1: `[1, 2, 4, 8]` (Standard)\n-   Path 2: `[1, 3, 9, 27]` (Wider spacing)\n-   Path 3: `[1, 1, 2, 2]` (Focus on local features)\n\nI will then concatenate the outputs of these parallel feature extractors. This creates a richer, multi-scale representation of the sequence. It's a \"poor man's attention mechanism\" or a simplified ensemble within the feature extractor itself. It directly addresses the \"inflexibility\" weakness I identified, is conceptually simple, and reuses proven components, minimizing the risk of implementation error.\n\nI will now go to the Research Counter and implement this \"Multi-Path DSConv\" experiment.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Multi-Path DSConv: Flexible Dilations to Challenge SOTA Backbone\"\ntags: \"dsconv,\
    \ multi-path, dilation, feature-extractor, backbone\"\nabstract: \"After reflection identified the fixed dilation pattern of the SOTA DSConv backbone as a key weakness, this experiment proposes a 'Multi-Path DSConv' feature extractor to create a more flexible architecture. Instead of a single deep stack of convolutions with one dilation schedule, this model uses multiple parallel, shallower DSConv stacks, each with a different dilation pattern. The outputs are concatenated to form a multi-scale representation. This tests the hypothesis that a richer set of features, capturing interactions at varied scales, will outperform the rigid, single-path backbone of the current SOTA.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001, 'd_model': 256, 'num_blocks_per_path': 2,\n          'kernel_size': 7, 'dropout_rate':\
    \ 0.1, 'tau': 0.25\n      }\n\n  # --- Shared Components ---\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int; kernel_size: int = 7; dilation: int = 1; dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h); h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,))(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  class DSConvPath(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]; kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = x\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              d = self.dilations[i % len(self.dilations)]\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model,\
    \ self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return h\n          \n  def lse_pool(h: jnp.ndarray, tau: float):\n      x = h / tau; m = jnp.max(x, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n      return tau * (jnp.log(jnp.mean(jnp.exp(x - m), axis=1) + 1e-12) + jnp.squeeze(m, axis=1))\n\n  # --- Main Network: Multi-Path DSConv Feature Extractor ---\n  class MultiPathDSConvNet(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model: int; num_blocks_per_path: int; \n      kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float; tau: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # Initial projection\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x); h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Define parallel paths with different dilation schedules\n          path1 = DSConvPath(self.d_model, self.num_blocks_per_path, [1, 2, 4, 8], self.kernel_size, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic)\n\
    \          path2 = DSConvPath(self.d_model, self.num_blocks_per_path, [1, 3, 9, 27], self.kernel_size, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic)\n          path3 = DSConvPath(self.d_model, self.num_blocks_per_path, [1, 1, 2, 2], self.kernel_size, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic)\n\n          # Concatenate path outputs\n          concatenated_features = jnp.concatenate([path1, path2, path3], axis=-1)\n          \n          # Project back to d_model\n          features_seq = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(concatenated_features)\n\n          # Use a simple, proven aggregator (Noema's Mean+Max) for a clean test of the backbone\n          mean_vec = jnp.mean(features_seq, axis=1)\n          max_vec = jnp.max(features_seq, axis=1)\n          fused = jnp.concatenate([mean_vec, max_vec], axis=-1)\n          \n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z); z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits =\
    \ nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          return logits.squeeze(-1) if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1 else logits\n\n  class NetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, model_instance): self.network = model_instance\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key); return self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if rng_key is None: rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0); return self.network.apply(params, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      model = MultiPathDSConvNet(**{k: v for k, v in hparams.items() if k in MultiPathDSConvNet.__annotations__}); return NetworkWrapper(model)\n```"
